# Cursor models only, until the next cycle

Set 27 Oct 2026. Applies to every Cursor session on this project until the owner says the usage cycle has reset. Then delete this rule and the matching sentence in `docs/workflow.md`.

Cursor models are Grok 4.7, Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5, and Composer 2.5. Claude, GPT, Gemini, and any other third-party model are off limits here, including when the user asks for a subagent, a review, or a faster model.

- This chat stays on a Cursor model. Do not suggest switching it to a third-party model.
- Subagents get an explicit Cursor model. Prefer Composer 2.5 for a mechanical brief, or Grok 4.7 with Fast off when the brief touches the generator, seeds, or saves. If the tool only lists Fast slugs, pass `grok-4.7-high-fast`.
- Do not pass `inherit` when the parent chat is a third-party model.
- Leave `.claude/agents/implementer.md` at `model: sonnet`. That line is for Claude Code, not for Cursor subagents.
